From 5984cb028f2144469e529542bf1b539ce14d783c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 03:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] refactor(perf+spine): one render clock, lazy corridor,
 coherent section spine

Smoothness
- lib/frame.ts: single shared rAF. Lenis and the Three.js corridor were
  running independent loops (requestAnimationFrame vs setAnimationLoop), so
  scroll and camera resolved in different frames and drifted under load.
  Both now subscribe to one clock, Lenis first. Loop stops when hidden.
- Corridor context loss now gates the tick instead of owning a private loop.

Speed
- Corridor is dynamically imported. Three.js (~700kb raw) left the initial
  bundle and now sits in its own deferred chunk, so the hero paints first.
- lib/useReducedMotion.ts via useSyncExternalStore. The old setState-in-effect
  pattern rendered a blank placeholder on the first pass, which meant the
  hero copy was not in the first paint at all. That was the LCP.
- Deleted 9 unused components plus the legacy index.html holding page.
  1460 lines removed, ~30% of the tree.
- Added the missing .gitignore.

Coherence
- Hero primary CTA pointed at #work, which was the services grid. The site's
  strongest promise delivered a price menu. Services grid is now #channels
  and the CTA points at #proof until case studies land.
- Hero badge no longer says 'Test transmission'.
- lib/motion.ts: one easing set, one duration scale, one reveal distance.
  Replaces four different y offsets and three eases.
- Process beat added, five steps, straight from the brief.
- lib/work.ts + /work/\[slug\] + WorkTeasers. Schema only, no invented
  clients or metrics. Section hides itself until real studies land.

Verified: tsc clean, eslint clean, next build passes, /work/[slug] SSG.
